    kind: work_item  # 2cdc
    title: "generate-schema hand-codes $defs + opaque metrics/limits/features blocks + omits top-level keys instead of introspecting dataclasses (docs/schema.json drift)"  # 2cdc
    status: todo_hard  # 2cdc
    priority: 1  # 2cdc
    parent:  # 2cdc
    tags:  # 2cdc
    - dogfood  # 2cdc
    - writer_contract  # 2cdc
    isbefore: []  # 2cdc
    duplicate_of: []  # 2cdc
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2cdc
    pr_ref:  # 2cdc
    description: "**Defect.** `docs/schema.json` is hand-maintained while claiming to be auto-generated, and has drifted from the actual dataclasses.\n\n**Mechanic.** `scripts/generate-schema` hand-codes the `$defs` as literal Python dicts (e.g. generate-schema:330 \"# Add Symbol definition (based on to_dict output)\"; :605-633 for AnalysisRun) and emits `limits`/`metrics`/`features` as bare untyped blocks at :203-212, rather than calling the existing `dataclass_to_json_schema` introspection helper (:88, uses `dataclasses.fields` at :94). The schema header nonetheless claims \"Auto-generated from Python dataclasses ... stays in sync with the code.\" The same hand-maintenance affects schema.py's reproducibility block.\n\n**Scope.** docs/schema.json. Symbol $def: 4 emitted fields absent from schema (discovery_language, display_label, protocol_origin, qualified_name, present on 34396/34396 nodes) and 1 dead schema-only field canonical_name emitted on 0/34396 nodes (not a dataclass field). AnalysisRun $def: 2 emitted fields absent (failed_files, pass_version, present on 84/84). Three top-level keys present in output but absent from schema properties (reproducibility_context, symbol_fingerprint_scheme, validation_report). Three top-level blocks emitted as opaque containers: metrics (7 keys), limits (10 keys), features (9 keys each, no Feature $def). Edge/Entrypoint/UsageContext $defs are clean.\n\n**Expectation.** Every $def and top-level block would be introspected from its dataclass via `dataclass_to_json_schema`, so the schema matches emitted fields exactly.\n\n**Fix.** Drive generate-schema (and schema.py's reproducibility block) from dataclass introspection via the existing `dataclass_to_json_schema` helper, rather than hand-coding $defs and opaque blocks.\n\n**Consequence.** Strict additionalProperties:false validation rejects every node (4 unknown axis fields) and every AnalysisRun (2 unknown fields); codegen produces a dead canonical_name accessor that is always None and no accessors for the real axis fields; metrics/limits/features get zero structural enforcement. A related internal-consistency facet of the same hand-maintained block: reproducibility_context.implications (schema.py:188-203) names pass_versions first as the field a consumer must match to assert functional identity, yet `captured` carries only {grammars, hypergumbo_version, python_implementation, python_version, tree_sitter_version} and never pass_versions — so a consumer following the documented reproducibility contract cannot detect a pass_version divergence.\n\n**Cross-refs.** This is the schema-generator root cause behind several individual undocumented-field findings (WI-ziguk validation_report absent from schema [wont_do], WI-sirir dev_frameworks/framework_mode, WI-mikin metrics.debug.profile_files_sum, and others). WI-mulub / WI-guvup / WI-romup are downstream registry/sub-schema-drift faces."  # 2cdc
    fields: {}  # 2cdc
